    "name": "Marionberry",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The Marionberry is&nbsp;a popular, thorny, trailing blackberry cultivar developed in Oregon, known for its rich, sweet-tart flavor, making it ideal for pies, jams, and fresh eating.&nbsp;It's a vigorous vine that requires a sturdy trellis for support and thrives in full sun, producing a heavy mid-summer crop.&nbsp;Proper pruning involves removing old, fruiting canes after harvest and training new canes to the support system.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by: Variious NW Growers</span></p>",
